{"seq":29,"at":"2026-10-22","kind":"printed","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w24577"},"reason":"Printed on publish-or-perish card pp-068, category 2; the card's own words are kept in cardText — \"[Astronomy] Which planet is known as the “Evening Star” due to its bright appearance?\nA. Mars  B. Jupiter  C. Venus\nAnswer: C. Venus is called the “Evening Star” when it is visible after sunset and the “Morning Star” when it appears before sunrise.\".","by":"merge art/architecture, art/design, art/painting, art/sculpture, belief/philosophy, belief/religion, belief/symbols, ear","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/publish-or-perish/pp-068.json","changes":[{"field":"en","new":"Which planet is known as the \"Evening Star\" when it shines brightly after sunset, and the \"Morning Star\" before sunrise?"},{"field":"de","new":"Welcher Planet wird „Abendstern“ genannt, wenn er nach Sonnenuntergang hell leuchtet, und „Morgenstern“ vor Sonnenaufgang?"},{"field":"origin","new":"printed"},{"field":"printed","new":{"source":"publish-or-perish","card":"pp-068","category":2}},{"field":"cardText","diff":[["+","[Astronomy] Which planet is known as the “Evening Star” due to its bright appearance?\nA. Mars  B. Jupiter  C. Venus\nAnswer: C. Venus is called the “Evening Star” when it is visible after sunset and the “Morning Star” when it appears before sunrise."]]},{"field":"fact","new":"f03947"}],"hash":"426da5a81b12"},
